==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Assault Unit R.E.I.''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Flight Unit R.E.I.''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Strike Unit R.E.I. is very well-balanced overall. She can be seen as the [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]] of [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating Cats]], except with lower viability outside of her specialization. Take note of R.E.I.'s high speed and below-average range (for an Uber Rare Cat), as she can put herself in peril against long-ranged enemies like [[Le'noir]] or go ahead of your meatshields. R.E.I. has the same range as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and should be protected well because of this.

Her immunity to [[Immune to Slow|Slow]] trivializes [[Queen B]] but has little usage elsewhere, as the only other non-collab Floating enemy that can slow is [[Bears Be Back]], which come with four other nasty effects and have the same range as R.E.I.; and the only stages to use [[Croakley]] with Floating enemies are [[Broadband Omens]] and [[False Resurrection]].

==='''True Form'''===
Flight Unit R.E.I. addressed her significant problem of attack rate, making her more usable as a generalist and against Floating enemies. Additionally, she is now [[Insanely Tough|Insanely Tough]] against Floating Enemies making it that much more likely for her to finish her attack before being interrupted. Overall, her True Form is a great improvement that makes her a considerably more valuable unit for a relatively cheap [[Catfruit]] cost.

==='''Talents'''===
Flight Unit R.E.I.'s first Talent of note is Freeze, which works particularly well for her; this ability has a very good chance of triggering at 40% as well as a very ideal freeze duration: any longer and enemies knocked back by her powerful attacks would return in her range after a second attack, which would be problematic. Immunity to Toxic makes her a very good counter to [[Gobble]], [[Zollow]] and [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]]. [[Survive]] is excellent too, as she has enough range to stay out of trouble for a good amount of time. As she relies on her stats to be of any use, the HP and Attack Buffs are also a good idea to get if you've already used [[Catseye]]s to boost her level.

